    Add the FastAPI server and a minimal streaming console
    
    A run takes minutes, so the HTTP interface is a stream rather than a
    request/response: POST /api/run returns server-sent events as each phase, tool
    call, test result and review lands. It consumes the same stream_run the CLI
    does, so there is one execution path and two renderings of it.
    
    GET /api/health runs the same preflight the CLI does, so a client can tell the
    user what is missing before a run rather than after. GET / serves a single-file
    console with the phase checklist and activity log, so the server is usable
    without a build step.
    
    A preflight failure and a mid-stream crash both arrive as error events rather
    than a broken connection or a 500 -- with a stream already open, an exception
    would otherwise reach the client as a truncated body with no explanation.
    
    225 tests pass.
    
